1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,240
Offering incentives requires that you understand the wants and needs of the person you're influencing.

2
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:11,400
This means that you'll likely use the receptive behaviors first to learn about the other's interests.

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:18,900
Once you're clear about them, you can then consider what options you have to fulfill that person's needs or respond to his or her interests.

4
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,900
In order to be influential, an incentive must be of interest to the other person.

5
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:29,500
You must be in control of it, and you must be willing to offer it in exchange for something that you value.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Incentives are not bribes.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
You can look at an incentive as a way to make a request or express need on your part by offering a fair deal to the other.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Here are some examples.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
If you'll agree to moving the deadline back by a week, I'll commit to providing you with the help you need to complete the work.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,500
You mentioned that you needed a speaker for the forum next month.

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:00,500
I'd be willing to do it if you'll spend an hour getting me up to speed on what you've done so far and some background on the participants.

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:10,500
I can't give you the additional full-time engineer you asked for, but I would be willing to provide funds for some consulting help on the project.

